msgid "How this workspace works"
msgstr "How this workspace works"

msgid ""
"This workspace holds six <strong>views</strong>, arranged in a grid. A map, "
"a chart and a table show data, and three <strong>selectors</strong> set the "
"period, org unit and data item they show. Views are linked through "
"<strong>channels</strong>. This tour follows one channel from start to end."
msgstr ""
"This workspace holds six <strong>views</strong>, arranged in a grid. A map, "
"a chart and a table show data, and three <strong>selectors</strong> set the "
"period, org unit and data item they show. Views are linked through "
"<strong>channels</strong>. This tour follows one channel from start to end."

msgid "View headers"
msgstr "View headers"

msgid ""
"Each view has a header with its name, its <strong>channel badges</strong>, "
"and buttons to maximize or close it. The demo starts with headers hidden, "
"for a cleaner first look. The <strong>Hide view headers</strong> option in "
"the <strong>Workspace</strong> tab turns them off again."
msgstr ""
"Each view has a header with its name, its <strong>channel badges</strong>, "
"and buttons to maximize or close it. The demo starts with headers hidden, "
"for a cleaner first look. The <strong>Hide view headers</strong> option in "
"the <strong>Workspace</strong> tab turns them off again."

msgid "Adding views"
msgstr "Adding views"

msgid ""
"The <strong>Add views</strong> tab offers up to 4 maps and visualizations, "
"as well as selectors and text. Click a tile, or drag it to where you want "
"it. Each view also gets its own <strong>settings tab</strong> in this strip."
msgstr ""
"The <strong>Add views</strong> tab offers up to 4 maps and visualizations, "
"as well as selectors and text. Click a tile, or drag it to where you want "
"it. Each view also gets its own <strong>settings tab</strong> in this strip."

msgid "Channels"
msgstr "Channels"

msgid ""
"A <strong>channel</strong> shares one value, here an org unit, between the "
"views linked to it. When one view sets it, the others follow. Each channel "
"has a letter and a color. This selector sets channel {{channel}}, shown as "
"<strong>Org unit {{channel}}</strong> above the tree."
msgstr ""
"A <strong>channel</strong> shares one value, here an org unit, between the "
"views linked to it. When one view sets it, the others follow. Each channel "
"has a letter and a color. This selector sets channel {{channel}}, shown as "
"<strong>Org unit {{channel}}</strong> above the tree."

msgid "Channel badges"
msgstr "Channel badges"

msgid ""
"A view's <strong>badges</strong> show the channels it belongs to. The map's "
"<strong>{{channel}}→←</strong> badge means it <strong>sets</strong> the "
"value when clicked (→) and <strong>follows</strong> it (←). The chart and "
"the table carry the same badge. Hover over a badge to see its value, or "
"click it to clear the value or leave the channel."
msgstr ""
"A view's <strong>badges</strong> show the channels it belongs to. The map's "
"<strong>{{channel}}→←</strong> badge means it <strong>sets</strong> the "
"value when clicked (→) and <strong>follows</strong> it (←). The chart and "
"the table carry the same badge. Hover over a badge to see its value, or "
"click it to clear the value or leave the channel."

msgid "Link settings"
msgstr "Link settings"

msgid ""
"Each view's settings tab has a <strong>Links</strong> section, with one row "
"per dimension. <strong>Channel</strong> selects the view's channel. "
"<strong>Set the value by clicking</strong> and <strong>Follow the "
"value</strong> define its role in it. <strong>When it follows</strong> "
"defines what it shows, for example Sub-units, or <strong>Highlight "
"only</strong>, which keeps the view's own periods or org units and marks "
"the value."
msgstr ""
"Each view's settings tab has a <strong>Links</strong> section, with one row "
"per dimension. <strong>Channel</strong> selects the view's channel. "
"<strong>Set the value by clicking</strong> and <strong>Follow the "
"value</strong> define its role in it. <strong>When it follows</strong> "
"defines what it shows, for example Sub-units, or <strong>Highlight "
"only</strong>, which keeps the view's own periods or org units and marks "
"the value."

msgid "Set the value"
msgstr "Set the value"

msgid ""
"<strong>Click {{highest}} on the map</strong>, and the map sets the value "
"of channel {{channel}}. Or press <strong>Next</strong>, and the demo clicks "
"it for you."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Click {{highest}} on the map</strong>, and the map sets the value "
"of channel {{channel}}. Or press <strong>Next</strong>, and the demo clicks "
"it for you."

msgid "The value travels"
msgstr "The value travels"

msgid ""
"The org unit tree is linked to channel {{channel}} too, so it "
"<strong>selects {{highest}}</strong>. Select another org unit in it, and "
"the map follows in turn."
msgstr ""
"The org unit tree is linked to channel {{channel}} too, so it "
"<strong>selects {{highest}}</strong>. Select another org unit in it, and "
"the map follows in turn."

msgid "Each view follows in its own way"
msgstr "Each view follows in its own way"

msgid ""
"The chart follows channel {{channel}} with <strong>Sub-units</strong>, set "
"under When it follows. Its districts become <strong>{{highest}}'s "
"chiefdoms</strong>. The table narrows to them too. The map, which set the "
"value, <strong>highlights</strong> it rather than redrawing."
msgstr ""
"The chart follows channel {{channel}} with <strong>Sub-units</strong>, set "
"under When it follows. Its districts become <strong>{{highest}}'s "
"chiefdoms</strong>. The table narrows to them too. The map, which set the "
"value, <strong>highlights</strong> it rather than redrawing."

msgid "A second channel"
msgstr "A second channel"

msgid ""
"Channel {{channel}} carries a period in the same way. <strong>Click a "
"month's name</strong> under the chart. The map shows that month, and the "
"table marks the quarter that contains it. Clicking a data point sets "
"<strong>both its month and its org unit</strong>."
msgstr ""
"Channel {{channel}} carries a period in the same way. <strong>Click a "
"month's name</strong> under the chart. The map shows that month, and the "
"table marks the quarter that contains it. Clicking a data point sets "
"<strong>both its month and its org unit</strong>."

msgid "Play through time"
msgstr "Play through time"

msgid ""
"The <strong>timeline</strong> sets channel {{channel}} one month at a time. "
"Press <strong>Play</strong>, and the map steps through the months, each "
"step waiting until the map has loaded. The chart and the table follow with "
"<strong>Highlight only</strong>. They keep their own periods, and mark the "
"current month, or the quarter that contains it."
msgstr ""
"The <strong>timeline</strong> sets channel {{channel}} one month at a time. "
"Press <strong>Play</strong>, and the map steps through the months, each "
"step waiting until the map has loaded. The chart and the table follow with "
"<strong>Highlight only</strong>. They keep their own periods, and mark the "
"current month, or the quarter that contains it."

msgid "Start again"
msgstr "Start again"

msgid "<strong>Reset the demo</strong> restores this layout at any time."
msgstr "<strong>Reset the demo</strong> restores this layout at any time."

msgid "Over to you"
msgstr "Over to you"

msgid ""
"Add a view, link it in its settings tab, and click to explore. The other "
"tour, <strong>The story</strong>, shows what these links reveal in the data."
msgstr ""
"Add a view, link it in its settings tab, and click to explore. The other "
"tour, <strong>The story</strong>, shows what these links reveal in the data."

