msgid "Malaria in Demoland"
msgstr "Malaria in Demoland"

msgid ""
"Malaria is endemic in Demoland, and its burden varies widely between "
"districts. <strong>Where is it highest, when, and why there?</strong> Three "
"<strong>linked views</strong>, a map, a chart and a table, answer it in a "
"few steps. A click in one updates the others. The data is synthetic, but "
"follows a pattern typical of endemic settings."
msgstr ""
"Malaria is endemic in Demoland, and its burden varies widely between "
"districts. <strong>Where is it highest, when, and why there?</strong> Three "
"<strong>linked views</strong>, a map, a chart and a table, answer it in a "
"few steps. A click in one updates the others. The data is synthetic, but "
"follows a pattern typical of endemic settings."

msgid "Where"
msgstr "Where"

msgid ""
"Malaria incidence, confirmed cases per 1,000 population per year. "
"<strong>{{highest}}</strong> has {{highestValue}}, <strong>{{ratio}} "
"times</strong> {{lowest}} ({{lowestValue}}). Incidence compares districts "
"of different population sizes, where case counts would mostly reflect "
"population."
msgstr ""
"Malaria incidence, confirmed cases per 1,000 population per year. "
"<strong>{{highest}}</strong> has {{highestValue}}, <strong>{{ratio}} "
"times</strong> {{lowest}} ({{lowestValue}}). Incidence compares districts "
"of different population sizes, where case counts would mostly reflect "
"population."

msgid "When"
msgstr "When"

msgid ""
"The same incidence by month, one line per district. Incidence rises with "
"the rainy season from May, but <strong>{{highest}} has the highest rate "
"every month</strong>. Seasonality alone does not explain its burden."
msgstr ""
"The same incidence by month, one line per district. Incidence rises with "
"the rainy season from May, but <strong>{{highest}} has the highest rate "
"every month</strong>. Seasonality alone does not explain its burden."

msgid "Select a district"
msgstr "Select a district"

msgid ""
"<strong>Click {{highest}} on the map</strong>, and the other views update "
"to {{highest}}. Or press <strong>Next</strong>, and the demo clicks it for "
"you."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Click {{highest}} on the map</strong>, and the other views update "
"to {{highest}}. Or press <strong>Next</strong>, and the demo clicks it for "
"you."

msgid "One click"
msgstr "One click"

msgid ""
"The map keeps every district in view and highlights {{highest}}. "
"<strong>The chart and the table now show {{highest}}'s chiefdoms</strong>, "
"and the org unit tree selects {{highest}}, without setting a filter in each "
"view."
msgstr ""
"The map keeps every district in view and highlights {{highest}}. "
"<strong>The chart and the table now show {{highest}}'s chiefdoms</strong>, "
"and the org unit tree selects {{highest}}, without setting a filter in each "
"view."

msgid "Drill down"
msgstr "Drill down"

msgid ""
"<strong>Right-click {{highest}}</strong> on the map, then choose "
"<strong>Drill down into {{highest}}</strong>. Or press "
"<strong>Next</strong>, and the demo drills down for you."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Right-click {{highest}}</strong> on the map, then choose "
"<strong>Drill down into {{highest}}</strong>. Or press "
"<strong>Next</strong>, and the demo drills down for you."

msgid "District-wide"
msgstr "District-wide"

msgid ""
"The map now shows {{highest}}'s <strong>{{count}} chiefdoms</strong>, with "
"the legend classes used for the districts. <strong>All of them fall in the "
"highest class</strong>, as {{highest}} does."
msgid_plural ""
"The map now shows {{highest}}'s <strong>{{count}} chiefdoms</strong>, with "
"the legend classes used for the districts. <strong>All of them fall in the "
"highest class</strong>, as {{highest}} does."
msgstr[0] ""
"The map now shows {{highest}}'s <strong>{{count}} chiefdoms</strong>, with "
"the legend classes used for the districts. <strong>All of them fall in the "
"highest class</strong>, as {{highest}} does."
msgstr[1] ""
"The map now shows {{highest}}'s <strong>{{count}} chiefdoms</strong>, with "
"the legend classes used for the districts. <strong>All of them fall in the "
"highest class</strong>, as {{highest}} does."

msgid "Not a single hotspot"
msgstr "Not a single hotspot"

msgid ""
"The chart has shown {{highest}}'s chiefdoms since the click. <strong>Each "
"stays above {{rate}} every month</strong>, the national rate for the year. "
"This points to a district-wide driver rather than a localized outbreak."
msgstr ""
"The chart has shown {{highest}}'s chiefdoms since the click. <strong>Each "
"stays above {{rate}} every month</strong>, the national rate for the year. "
"This points to a district-wide driver rather than a localized outbreak."

msgid "Why"
msgstr "Why"

msgid ""
"The table has narrowed to {{highest}}'s chiefdoms too. In {{quarter}}, none "
"of its {{count}} reaches the {{target}}% coverage target for the third dose "
"of the malaria vaccine. <strong>Where the malaria burden is highest, "
"vaccine coverage is lowest.</strong>"
msgid_plural ""
"The table has narrowed to {{highest}}'s chiefdoms too. In {{quarter}}, none "
"of its {{count}} reaches the {{target}}% coverage target for the third dose "
"of the malaria vaccine. <strong>Where the malaria burden is highest, "
"vaccine coverage is lowest.</strong>"
msgstr[0] ""
"The table has narrowed to {{highest}}'s chiefdoms too. In {{quarter}}, none "
"of its {{count}} reaches the {{target}}% coverage target for the third dose "
"of the malaria vaccine. <strong>Where the malaria burden is highest, "
"vaccine coverage is lowest.</strong>"
msgstr[1] ""
"The table has narrowed to {{highest}}'s chiefdoms too. In {{quarter}}, none "
"of its {{count}} reaches the {{target}}% coverage target for the third dose "
"of the malaria vaccine. <strong>Where the malaria burden is highest, "
"vaccine coverage is lowest.</strong>"

msgid "From where to why, in two clicks"
msgstr "From where to why, in two clicks"

msgid ""
"A dashboard filter changes every item the same way. Here the views follow "
"the analyst's questions. <strong>One click moved every view to "
"{{highest}}</strong>, and each kept its role, from context to trend to "
"coverage. With channels, <strong>two districts or two periods can be "
"compared side by side</strong>, which one dashboard filter cannot do. The "
"other tour, <strong>How it works</strong>, explains the links."
msgstr ""
"A dashboard filter changes every item the same way. Here the views follow "
"the analyst's questions. <strong>One click moved every view to "
"{{highest}}</strong>, and each kept its role, from context to trend to "
"coverage. With channels, <strong>two districts or two periods can be "
"compared side by side</strong>, which one dashboard filter cannot do. The "
"other tour, <strong>How it works</strong>, explains the links."

